  'draft', 'foundation',
  $x$A 44-year-old woman with known Addison's disease is brought to the emergency department by ambulance after three days of vomiting and diarrhoea due to a viral gastroenteritis. She has been unable to take her usual oral hydrocortisone. On arrival she is drowsy, with BP 78/46 mmHg, HR 128 bpm, temperature 35.9C. Capillary glucose is 3.1 mmol/L. Blood tests show sodium 126 mmol/L and potassium 6.4 mmol/L.$x$,
  'What is the most appropriate immediate management?',
  array['Addisonian crisis','adrenal insufficiency','emergency']
),
